+	<TEXT>
+		<Tag>TXT_KEY_CONCEPT_SAS_SEVOPEDIA_NUMTXT_LEGEND_PEDIA</Tag>
+		<English>[H1]Sevopedia numTxt Legend[\H1][PARAGRAPH:2]This page explains abbreviated labels shown under icon buttons in Sevopedia Building, Unit, Terrain, and Feature pages.[PARAGRAPH:2][H2]Building page numTxt[\H2][PARAGRAPH:2]- InC: required in city (the prerequisite building must be in the same city).[PARAGRAPH:2]- R: world-size requirement modifier (not random). This is the same R used inside AC N+R.[PARAGRAPH:2]- AC N+R: required in all cities. N = base XML requirement, R = world-size requirement modifier from World Size iBuildingClassPrereqModifier (rounded up). [PARAGRAPH:2]- Example for AC with N=2: Duel/Tiny (modifier 0) => 2; Standard (+38) => 3; Huge (+75) => 4.[PARAGRAPH:2]- ACs: applies to all cities.[PARAGRAPH:2]- AUC: applies to all eligible unit classes/combats.[PARAGRAPH:2]- (!)Cvc: this prerequisite can be bypassed or altered by civic rules.[PARAGRAPH:2]- OR: alternative prerequisite grouping; one of the OR-linked icons can satisfy that part.[PARAGRAPH:2]- Plain number (for example 1, 2, 3): exact count linked to that icon (for example free specialists count).[PARAGRAPH:2]- FBBR (when shown alone for free bonus count): world-size dependent free bonus count (iNumFreeBuildingBonuses). In this mod, for example: Standard=4, Huge=6.[PARAGRAPH:2][H2]Unit/Terrain/Feature page numTxt[\H2][PARAGRAPH:2]- +A/+D: attack and defense percent modifiers.[PARAGRAPH:2]- +A/_: attack-only modifier.[PARAGRAPH:2]- _/+D: defense-only modifier.[PARAGRAPH:2]- _/_: no attack/defense modifier.[PARAGRAPH:2]- +X%: single percent modifier (for example combat-class modifier).[PARAGRAPH:2]- N: unit has free Navigator promotion.[PARAGRAPH:2]- HM1, HM2, HM3: unit has free Hills Master tier 1/2/3. Contiguous tiers use ranges (for example HM1-3); gaps keep addition (for example HM1+3).[PARAGRAPH:2]- W1, W2, W3: unit has free Woodsman tier 1/2/3. Combined forms (for example W1+2+3) indicate multiple free tiers.</English>
+	</TEXT>
+	<TEXT>
+		<Tag>TXT_KEY_CONCEPT_SAS_SEVOPEDIA_CATEGORIES_LEGEND</Tag>
+		<English>Sevopedia Categories Legend</English>
+	</TEXT>
+	<TEXT>
+		<Tag>TXT_KEY_CONCEPT_SAS_SEVOPEDIA_CATEGORIES_LEGEND_PEDIA</Tag>
+		<English>[H1]Sevopedia Categories Legend[\H1][PARAGRAPH:2]This page explains shortened category labels used in the left Sevopedia category list.[PARAGRAPH:2]- Improv.: Improvements.[PARAGRAPH:2]- Un. List: Unit List.[PARAGRAPH:2]- Un. Tree: Unit Upgrade Tree.[PARAGRAPH:2]- Pr. List: Promotion List.[PARAGRAPH:2]- Pr. Tree: Promotion Tree.[PARAGRAPH:2]- N. Wond.: National Wonders.[PARAGRAPH:2]- W. Wond.: World Wonders.[PARAGRAPH:2]- W. Sizes: World Sizes.[PARAGRAPH:2]- Corporat.: Corporations.[PARAGRAPH:2]- Outdated: legacy/reference pages kept for compatibility/history.[PARAGRAPH:2]- Mods Info: custom AdvCiv-SAS concept pages and legends.[PARAGRAPH:2]Labels are shortened mainly to fit sidebar width cleanly at different resolutions and UI scales.</English>
+	</TEXT>
+	<TEXT>
+		<Tag>TXT_KEY_CONCEPT_SAS_SEVOPEDIA_SPEED_CHART_LEGEND</Tag>
+		<English>Sevopedia Speed Chart Legend</English>
+	</TEXT>
+	<TEXT>
+		<Tag>TXT_KEY_CONCEPT_SAS_SEVOPEDIA_SPEED_CHART_LEGEND_PEDIA</Tag>
+		<English>[H1]Sevopedia Speed Chart Legend[\H1][PARAGRAPH:2]This page explains abbreviated labels used in the Sevopedia Game Speed chart.[PARAGRAPH:2]- Inc Y XX: increments years chunk XX.[PARAGRAPH:2]- Inc M XX: increments months chunk XX.[PARAGRAPH:2]- Cal XX: calendar row XX.[PARAGRAPH:2]- S XX (N%): summary row XX at N percent of total turns.</English>
 	</TEXT>
 </Civ4GameText>
