 ### UI (In-game)
 
-- **Worker recommendation highlights disabled**: turned off tile coloring for "worker-recommended plot to improve" (in `CvGame::updateColoredPlots` within `CvGameInterface.cpp`). Reasons: (1) avoids extra computation in both debug ([see for related info this autoplay info](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/Modding_Ressources/README.md#how-to-autoplay-let-the-ai-play-for-you-super-fast-gameplay--testing-tool-in-map-loaded-save-file-new-game-etc-view)) and normal play; (2) our worker logic now relies on `CvUnitAI::AI_bestCityBuild`, so the vanilla highlight often disagrees and can mislead; (3) the highlight was easily confused with **city site** recommendations. City-site suggestions remain enabled and intentionally prominent; in practice, they frequently pick **strong** locations—quite often as good as, or better than, typical manual choices. See [Settlers (AI)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md#settlers-ai). *Note:* the **displayed recommended settle city plots** don’t always match what the AI would settle if it were playing your civ in autoplay; the UI hint path may be (not sure) using a different logic from the reworked/optimized `AIFoundValue::evaluate`. Treat them as general information, not guarantees.
-- **Beautified** the **Domestic Advisor** (F1 key) (now shows in "Producing" column the **button (i.e. icon) of the current item being built** (unit, building, project, process)) and updated its dimensions so it occupies the **full game window width** and more elements are visible (Espionage slider, HUD, selected units row(s)). Change in [CvDomesticAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvDomesticAdvisor.py). See [Main Advisors reworks](/README.md#main-advisors-reworks-eg-score-tab-history-tab-in-the-info-screen-advisor).
-- **Enlarged, excentered the Foreign Advisor**'s (F4 key) screen, and refined its tabs so they can display **up to 12 players** and **overall more information** so **less scrolling** is needed while still **preserving key relevant information** for display (scoreboard, map, commerce sliders and values, etc.). The code was also refactored to improve **dynamic scaling**, ensuring most UI elements automatically realign if dimensions are changed in [CvForeignAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvForeignAdvisor.py) and [CvExoticForeignAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvExoticForeignAdvisor.py). Notably renamed the Active tab to **Treaties** tab (no longer shows redundant bonuses (since their deal can be cancelled from the bonuses tab)), and **beautified** it with **icons**.
-- Did a similar rework of the **Military Advisor** (F5 key) in [CvMilitaryAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMilitaryAdvisor.py) now expanded and with **Unit Combat and Units buttons** (i.e. icons); also reworked the **Technology Advisor** (F6 key) in [CvTechChooser.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvTechChooser.py).
-- Did a similar rework of the **Info Screen** (F9 key) in [CvInfoScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvInfoScreen.py); in particular in **Top 5 Cities** we now use a multilist to display more wonders in a prettier way, and in the **Wonders** tab we now **show the Wonders' Buttons** (i.e. icons) in the first column (**click to move to city** mechanic is moved to the City column instead); the **Statistics** tab now also shows buttons (plus **change default ordering** from alphabetical to **from most to least Built/Current** (avoids tedious manual user ordering each time)), and the **Graph** Tab and possibly other tabs also show buttons (e.g., **leader icons before text**, **emojis**). Also added other information (e.g., turn numbers in the Graph tab).
-- Additionally, added in the **Info Screen** (F9 key) a new **History Tab**, showing a **text-colored spoiler-free** account of the key moments that happened each turn. Based on the **ReplayScreen**'s text, so **preserves information on save reload** unlike the Event Log. Optional **LOG button** allows to export to `PythonDbg.log` text file the output, and has optional **caching** for performance. Change in [CvInfoScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvInfoScreen.py). See [README.md: History Tab](/README.md#history-tab-in-the-info-screen-advisor).
-- Added in the **Info Screen** (F9 key) a new **Score Tab** showing a **sortable (default ordered by highest score) table** with all relevant scoreboard fields, plus **new fields** like Player ID (to distinguish identical Name/Civ/Leader/Player Color), Player color, total Power (of a player, distinct from power ratios), total Power per City, Land%, V/M. Added a clickable **"Legend"** text that **redirects to Sevopedia Concepts' "Score Tab Columns" page**. Note that unlike military ratios, PowT and PoT/C are shown even for the human player, since these vary every turn. If table has more than max rows, table expands and Legend link moves to top right. Change in [CvInfoScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvInfoScreen.py). See [README.md: Score Tab](/README.md#score-tab-in-the-info-screen-advisor).
-- Beautified the **Victory Screen** (F8 key) in [CvVictoryScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvVictoryScreen.py): **added Buttons/Icons** (Leaders, Religions, Apostolic Palace, UN, Spaceship parts, Traits as chars, etc.), **Thousands Separators**, **Victory Culture Percentages** (mirroring the changes in [CvInfoScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvInfoScreen.py)).
-- Added **"Willing to become vassal"** and **"Vassal"** **icons** in the Foreign Advisor's Glance tab in the human player's row, to help avoid the need to tediously check these up through other screens, in [CvExoticForeignAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvExoticForeignAdvisor.py), and in [CvDLLWidgetData.cpp](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvDLLWidgetData.cpp) for the corresponding **tooltip** (on hover). See ["Willing to become a vassal" and "vassal" icons](/README.md#willing-to-become-a-vassal-and-vassal-icons-in-foreign-advisors-glance-tab).
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5531+) **Beautified** and **expanded**, and add **support for text upscaling** for miscallenous **screens**: [CvDawnOfMan.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvDawnOfMan.py) ("The sun rises on the Year" greeting new game screen) is **expanded laterally and vertically** to **avoid scrolling**, add **icons** for buildings and units, add icon **chars for traits**; [CvTechSplashScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvTechSplashScreen.py) (when a new tech is discovered)  is moderately **expanded** to **avoid scrolling**, vertically center screen (was slightly excentered); [CvHallOfFameScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvHallOfFameScreen.py) is **maximized to full screen** with enlarged columns; [CvReplayScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvReplayScreen.py) is **maximized to full screen**; [CvDanQuayle.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvDanQuayle.py) ("you have displayed the leadership abilities" post-game screen) is **maximized to full screen** and has a **greatly expanded leader NIF** and **maximized vertically score table** to **avoid scrolling**. See [README.md (Miscallenous screens)](/README.md#miscallenous-screens)
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5517+) **Reorganized advisors**: **merged** the **espionage** screen into the **Foreign Advisor**, the **Economic Advisor's Finance Tab** into the **Domestic Advisor**, the **Economic Advisor's Environment Tab** into the **Info Screen**, the **Religion** Advisor and **Corporation** Advisor (so it is always visible and easier to access) into the new **Policy Advisor**; so they are now **tabs of these instead** (deleted the old now obsolete lone advisor .py files); **swap advisors**: **Victory screen** to F9 and **Info Screen** to F8 so the Info Screen is easier to split to F7 and F8 later on and so layout is **more logically organized** from internal to external advisors; **split advisors**: the **Foreign Advisor** is now split into **Foreign Trade Advisor (F4)** (TREATIES, BONUSES, TECHS, CITIES), and **Foreign Diplomacy Advisor (F3)** (RELATIONS, GLANCE, INFO, ESPIONAGE) as it **was crowded** to reduce the need for **tab navigation** and for **clearer thematic differentiation**, using a shell (i.e. almost empty file for **linking only**) [CvForeignDiplomacyAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvForeignDiplomacyAdvisor.py) file for the 2nd advisor.
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5524+) Rearrange Advisor **keyboard shortcuts** (in [CIV4ControlInfos.xml](/Assets/XML/Units/CIV4ControlInfos.xml) and DLL files like [CvEnums.h](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvEnums.h), [CvEnums.h](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvEnums.h), [CvGameInterface.cpp](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvGameInterface.cpp), and [CyEnumsInterface.cpp](/CvGameCoreDLL/CyEnumsInterface.cpp)) and adjust the **order of advisor buttons** in map view and **Sevopedia shortcuts** corresponding text to match the advisors changes.
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5521+) **Expand** and most **advisors** so they scale to **game resolution dynamically** instead of hardcoded advisor screen dimensions. The code was also refactored to improve **dynamic scaling**, ensuring **most UI elements automatically realign** if dimensions are changed. Advisors are now **excentered** so **overall more information** is displayed, thus **reducing the need for scrolling**, while still **preserving key relevant information** for display (scoreboard, map, commerce sliders and values, etc.). Some of their dimensions are **harmonized**. Note: some **right space for scoreboard** and **top space for the top bars** of the main interface was made (since commerce sliders are now as of now on the right side, they don't need left space anymore). See [Main Advisors reworks](/README.md#main-advisors-reworks-eg-score-tab-timeline-tab-in-the-info-screen-advisor)
+- **Beautified** the **Domestic Advisor**: now shows the **button (i.e. icon) of the current item being built** (unit, building, project, process) in "Producing" column. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5522+) Use the **shared advisor shell layout** (**top/bottom bars** + single content panel, remove the old exit icon) so Domestic Advisor **mirrors other advisors' structure** instead of a floating table, now using a **clearer constrast dark yellow theme** instead. Make the advisor be a tab as the **Overview** tab. Change in [CvDomesticAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvDomesticAdvisor.py).
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5528+) Minor **beautified** the [CvCustomizableDomesticAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvCustomizableDomesticAdvisor.py): increase **legend culture text width** so it is not cramped when upscaled. Note: although it is functional, the Custom Domestic Advisor is **not supported** in AdvCiv-SAS as of now, so it is lacking the Finance Tab.
